---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
export function getStaticPaths(){return ['second-claude-account','claude-desktop','codex-desktop','custom-icons','troubleshooting','privacy'].map(slug=>({params:{slug}}));}
const content={
 'second-claude-account':{title:'Use a second Claude account on Windows without logging out',intro:'Claude Desktop keeps one account signed in at a time. Here is how to keep a personal and a work account open side by side, and switch with one click.',sections:[['Why Claude Desktop logs you out','Claude Desktop stores your login, conversations and settings in one data folder on your PC. Signing in to another account replaces the first one, because both would share that folder.'],['The fix: one data folder per account','Give each account its own data folder and Claude Desktop treats them as separate installs. Hatrack does this for you: install it, choose Create profile, select Claude Desktop, name the profile (for example Work), and open it. Sign in to your second account in that window. Your first account is untouched.'],['Switch accounts in one click','Each profile gets its own Desktop and Start Menu shortcut and its own taskbar icon in a colour you choose. Click the one you need. Both can be open at the same time, so there is nothing to sign out of.'],['Other ways, and their limits','Signing out and back in works but costs time on every switch. Browser profiles keep several accounts open, but only for claude.ai on the web. Separate Windows users keep accounts apart, but you can only use one at a time. Hand-made shortcuts with the --user-data-dir flag work, but their windows merge on the taskbar and are easy to break.'],['What this preview verifies','Separate data folders and separate taskbar identities are implemented and tested. Independent sign-in across Claude Desktop updates is still going through acceptance checks, and Hatrack asks once before opening a profile on an untested Claude version.']]},
 'claude-desktop':{title:'Run multiple Claude Desktop accounts on Windows',intro:'Keep personal, work, and client desktop sessions in separate local folders, with recognisable launchers.',sections:[['How to create a profile','Open Hatrack, choose Create profile, select Claude Desktop, and enter a name. Choose an icon and your shortcuts, create the profile, then launch it and sign in. New profiles do not inherit your original login.'],['Automatic detection and manual selection','Hatrack looks for the registered Claude Windows package and standard locations. If it is missing, use the official download link. If detection misses an installed copy, use Locate app and select the official Claude desktop executable.'],['Existing profiles','Find existing profiles lists candidate folders. Import only the correct profile; original shortcuts are preserved. The same vendor executable may serve multiple profiles, while their local data folders remain separate.'],['What is verified?','The preview implements separate user-data and cache launch arguments. Independent authenticated sessions, restart persistence, and vendor-update behaviour require recorded acceptance before stable compatibility is claimed.']]},
 'codex-desktop':{title:'Run multiple Codex Desktop accounts on Windows',intro:'Codex Desktop needs both its desktop state and agent home separated. A CLI configuration profile alone is not enough.',sections:[['Desktop, not CLI','Select Codex Desktop in Hatrack. The ordinary ChatGPT desktop installation and Codex CLI are different applications. Packaged Codex can use a desktop executable named ChatGPT.exe; Hatrack checks its desktop resources and metadata.'],['How isolation is configured','Each new profile gets its own CODEX_HOME, CODEX_ELECTRON_USER_DATA_PATH, and Chromium user-data directory. Profile configuration uses file-based credential storage. Credentials are not copied from the default session.'],['Importing an existing home','The original .codex home cannot be adopted. Imported homes must explicitly select file credential storage. Browser state from an old launcher may not be present, so sign-in can be required again.'],['Compatibility gate','Desktop override behaviour is version-dependent. This preview is not certified for independent authenticated accounts. Two simultaneous sign-ins, sign-out independence, restart persistence, and unchanged original state are mandatory release checks. WSL and managed authentication policies need separate validation.']]},
 'custom-icons':{title:'Custom colours and icons for desktop profiles',intro:'Recolour the Claude or Codex app logo, or upload your own image.',sections:[['Choose a built-in design','Choose the matching Claude or Codex desktop logo. Pick a preset, use the RGB colour picker, or enter a hex value. Recolouring preserves the original logo silhouette. The Hatrack logo remains separate.'],['Upload your own image','PNG, JPEG, and ICO images are decoded locally. Use images at most 10 MB and 4096 pixels per side. Adjust image size, padding, horizontal and vertical crop, and background while checking the previews.'],['Desktop and taskbar consistency','Hatrack generates multiple icon sizes and uses the same artwork across its shortcuts and profile windows. Reopen a running profile after editing its icon. Windows may require unpinning and repinning an old taskbar shortcut.']]},
 'troubleshooting':{title:'Desktop detection and launch troubleshooting',intro:'Fix a missing location or a failed launch without resetting valuable profile data.',sections:[['The installed app is not detected','Choose Locate desktop app, select Claude or Codex, and browse to its official desktop executable. Hatrack rejects CLI tools and profile-launcher stubs. Package discovery is preferable for WindowsApps because Windows restricts folder browsing.'],['Another program is currently using this file','Windows app-package updates or stale runtime state can prevent Claude from launching. Save your work, finish vendor updates, and restart Windows if the error persists. Hatrack does not kill unrelated services or reset authentication data to work around this upstream failure.'],['A shortcut name already exists','Choose another name. Hatrack refuses to overwrite an unrelated shortcut and rolls back incomplete creation. Renaming a managed profile keeps its permanent identity and data folder.'],['Codex rejects the credential store','An imported Codex home must set cli_auth_credentials_store = "file" at the top level of config.toml. Hatrack does not rewrite imported configuration. Organisation policies may prevent this change; do not bypass them.'],['Reporting an issue','Include Windows, Hatrack, and vendor desktop versions and reproducible steps. Use the local diagnostics export, which omits credentials and profile paths. Never attach auth.json, cookies, private conversations, or account tokens.']]},
 'privacy':{title:'Local data, privacy, and ownership',intro:'Hatrack is your local organiser, not another account or a cloud service.',sections:[['What stays on your computer','Profile metadata, icons, and new app-state directories are stored under your local Hatrack folder. No Hatrack telemetry or credential upload is implemented. Vendor apps and your browser retain their own networking and privacy behaviour.'],['Removal keeps account data','Removing a launcher deletes its library entry and owned shortcuts, while retaining profile folders. Uninstalling Hatrack preserves the catalogue and profile data. Reinstall and save a profile to recreate its shortcuts.'],['Ownership and MIT','Hatrack is a personal project by Muneef Mumthas. Original software and artwork use the MIT licence, which permits modification and commercial redistribution with the notice retained. Dependencies, vendor app logos, and product names retain their own rights. The website saves only your appearance preference in local browser storage.'],['The boundary of isolation','Separate local state is not an operating-system sandbox. Profiles run as the same Windows user and external integrations can share state. Use separate Windows users if you need a stronger security boundary.']]}
};
const page=content[Astro.params.slug as keyof typeof content];
---
<Layout title={`${page.title} | Hatrack`} description={page.intro}><article class="article"><h1>{page.title}</h1><p class="lead">{page.intro}</p>{page.sections.map(([heading,text])=><section><h2>{heading}</h2><p>{text}</p></section>)}</article></Layout>
